\DOC GEN_PROVE_SAFETY_SPEC_TAC

\TYPE {GEN_PROVE_SAFETY_SPEC_TAC : term list -> tactic -> thm * (thm option array) -> thm list -> ((thm * (thm option array)) -> string -> tactic) -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Fully discharges an existentially quantified constant-time/safety specification
goal, leaving no subgoals.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes five arguments: a {term list} naming the variables treated as
public; a {tactic} performing preparatory/expansion work on the goal (here
expanding register-set {MAYCHANGE} components); a pair
{thm * (thm option array)} packaging the program's length theorem with a
per-instruction decoding table; a {thm list} of extra rewrite theorems applied
to the loaded-bytes hypothesis; and a function {(thm * (thm option array)) ->
string -> tactic} that builds the single-stepping tactic from that pair. It
applies to an assumption-free goal of the form {?- ?f. !x1 ... xn. t ==>
ensures ...}, whose postcondition asserts the existence of an event trace equal
to {f x1 ... xn} and constrained by a memory-access bound, and proves it
outright:
{
   ?- ?f. !x1 ... xn. t ==> ensures ...
   =====================================  GEN_PROVE_SAFETY_SPEC_TAC pubvars prep (lenth, decode) rewrites mkstep
                                          (no subgoals)
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces there is only this single outcome: goals with no
assumptions, all of the above existential {ensures} shape, always closed
completely.

\ENDDOC
